// Commonwealth Mandatory Withdrawal Schedule (§20.8) — DATA.
//
// Transcribed verbatim from the [4.43a] "Commonwealth Land Unit Reinforcement and Withdrawal
// Schedule", PDF p114–115 (read 2026-09-13). This file holds only the WITHDRAWAL ("WD:") entries;
// the arrival ("reinforcement") and "Rtn:" (return) entries of the same chart are handled by the
// reinforcement schedule (scenario `reinforcements` + OB `Arrival::Turn`).
//
// Per the chart legend (p115):
//   * `game_turn` / `ops_stage` = the Game-Turn and Operations Stage on which the withdrawal MUST
//     be performed (§20.83). The units must be at Cairo or Alexandria at ≥75% max TOE by then
//     (§20.82/§20.85), or they are eliminated (§20.83) and may not return.
//   * `tpt` = (truck_value_points, motorization_points) that must accompany the withdrawal (the
//     chart's "Tpt: a/b"). Truck Value Points: 1 Light = ½, 1 Medium = 1, 1 Heavy = 2.
//   * `units` = the verbatim withdrawal text. Bracketed tokens are the parent formation / nationality
//     (SIZE: Div/Bde/Bn/Coy; NAT: In=Indian, Aus=Australian, NZ=New Zealand, SA=South African, no
//     nationality = British). "[Less …]" excludes the named sub-formations; "any N …" is a §20.81
//     by-type choice left to the Commonwealth player (§20.82: pick units at ≥75% TOE).
//
// This is transcription, not interpretation — the runtime unit binding (mapping each entry to the
// scenario OB's units) is a separate concern; see docs/deferred-items.md AU24.
